From bdec50840399e26dd10d90f78f6eb7073450f37d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:00:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Zygote: Synchronize non-root child cgroup setup

WebView and App zygotes cannot prepare their children's process cgroups.
Their child specialization races system_server's creation and delegation
of the target UID's scheduling files, and may abort with EACCES while
still running as the zygote UID.

Return a one-shot pipe with the PID for explicit child-zygote requests.
Wait at the target UID until system_server acknowledges completed setup,
then apply the existing scheduler profile. Have the matching root zygote
perform creation and ownership delegation: system_server retains its
original capabilities and cannot chown scheduling files to another UID.
Authenticate its socket SID and restrict the target to an isolated UID
in a still-specializing descendant of that zygote.

Have the child acknowledge its target UID to its parent before the PID
is returned. Otherwise delegation can race setresuid and reject a valid
child before it reaches the existing setup gate. Bound this first phase
by the existing child-start timeout and keep every identity check.

Close both ends on every exit; EOF, invalid acknowledgements and failed
setup cannot launch the child. Keep regular zygote, USAP and system_server
specialization ordering intact.

Signed-off-by: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
